  "summary": "libpcap BPF interpreter treats the offset in the 'ja L' BPF instruction as a signed integer to implement looping via…",
  "details": "libpcap BPF interpreter treats the offset in the 'ja L' BPF instruction as a signed integer to implement looping via backward jumps, but it does not limit the number of loop iterations.  A crafted filter program or the 'protochain' primitive used on a crafted network packet can cause the interpreter to loop infinitely.",
